<h1>The agent harness, <em>mapped</em>.</h1>
<p class="lede">How an AI agent works in my vault: it enters through the rules, finds its plan or makes one with me, works in a loop under a guard and my yes, and leaves what it learned for the next plan.</p>
<p class="hint">Scroll the map sideways to see it whole.</p>
<div class="explore"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-0" checked aria-label="No step open"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-1" aria-label="Step 1: Enter through the desk"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-2" aria-label="Step 2: Find the work"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-3" aria-label="Step 3: No plan yet: define, then plan"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-4" aria-label="Step 4: Work in a loop"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-5" aria-label="Step 5: Hooks keep the thread"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-6" aria-label="Step 6: Capture, then triage"><input class="st-r" type="radio" name="step" id="st-7" aria-label="Step 7: The vault learns">
<figure class="map" style="margin-left:0;margin-right:0"><div class="map__in"><svg class="harness" viewBox="0 0 1240 780" role="img" aria-labelledby="hm-t hm-d" font-family="IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif"><title id="hm-t">The Aevifex harness: how an agent works</title><desc id="hm-d">An agent starts and reads AGENTS.md, the rules, then PINNED.md, the router. If the work has a plan, it goes to the office, where the plan sits with its memory, its record and its pointer, now.md; if not, the define-project skill gathers context and interviews Marc, and the planning skill writes the plan. From the pointer the agent starts working, one step of the plan at a time, in a loop: in Claude Code each command, write and web call passes a guard, run by a hook; the checks run; nothing is committed, merged or sent without Marc's yes, and the gate keeps private data out of what leaves; each turn is recorded, and hooks save the transcript around a compaction and call the note-taker, which keeps the plan's memory. Then the next step, until the plan is done. Loose ends go to the inbox as one line each, and so do Marc's own ideas to improve the system; every Monday the triage skill drains it with Marc's yes into NEXUS, his second brain, which feeds the next plan.</desc><defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M1 1.5L8.5 5 1 8.5" fill="none" data-ps="c-9c9284" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></marker><marker id="ahh" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M1 1.5L8.5 5 1 8.5" fill="none" data-ps="c-b8561a" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></marker><marker id="ahl" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8.5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M1 1.5L8.5 5 1 8.5" fill="none" data-ps="c-336f7e" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" str